{"id":"mahabharata-12-306","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":306,"title":"षडधिकत्रिशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 306 · Yajnavalkya and Vishvavasu","summary":{"en":"Yajnavalkya answers Janaka's question about the supreme beyond the unmanifest and tells of his meeting with the Gandharva Vishvavasu, who put to him questions on the nature of time, the unborn and the one who is both. The adhyaya ends with the praise that Yajnavalkya gave to King Janaka a teaching, the undying and sorrowless nectar.","kn":"ಅವ್ಯಕ್ತದ ಆಚೆಯ ಪರಮದ ಬಗ್ಗೆ ಜನಕನ ಪ್ರಶ್ನೆಗೆ ಯಾಜ್ಞವಲ್ಕ್ಯ ಉತ್ತರಿಸಿ, ಗಂಧರ್ವ ವಿಶ್ವಾವಸು ಕಾಲ, ಅಜ, ಎರಡೂ ಆದವನ ಬಗ್ಗೆ ಪ್ರಶ್ನೆ ಕೇಳಿದ ಭೇಟಿಯನ್ನು ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಯಾಜ್ಞವಲ್ಕ್ಯ ಜನಕನಿಗೆ ನೀಡಿದ ಅಮರ, ಶೋಕರಹಿತ ಉಪನಿಷತ್ತಿನ ಶ್ಲಾಘನೆಯಿಂದ ಅಧ್ಯಾಯ ಮುಗಿಯುತ್ತದೆ.","hi":"याज्ञवल्क्य अव्यक्त से परे परम के बारे में जनक के प्रश्न का उत्तर देते हैं और गन्धर्व विश्वावसु से अपनी भेंट बताते हैं जिसने काल, अज और दोनों रूप वाले के बारे में प्रश्न किए। अध्याय याज्ञवल्क्य के जनक को दिए अमर, शोकरहित उपनिषद् की प्रशंसा पर समाप्त होता है।","te":"అవ్యక్తానికి అతీతమైన పరమం గురించి జనకుని ప్రశ్నకు యాజ్ఞవల్క్యుడు బదులిచ్చి, గంధర్వుడు విశ్వావసు కాలం, అజం, రెండూ అయినవాని గురించి అడిగిన కలయికను చెబుతాడు. యాజ్ఞవల్క్యుడు జనకునికి ఇచ్చిన అమర, శోకరహిత ఉపనిషత్తు ప్రశంసతో అధ్యాయం ముగుస్తుంది.","ta":"வெளிப்படாததற்கு அப்பாற்பட்ட பரம் பற்றிய ஜனகனின் கேள்விக்கு யாஜ்ஞவல்க்யர் பதிலளித்து, காலம், பிறப்பற்றது, இரண்டுமானது பற்றிக் கேட்ட கந்தர்வன் விஸ்வாவசுவுடனான சந்திப்பைக் கூறுகிறார். யாஜ்ஞவல்க்யர் ஜனகனுக்கு அளித்த அழிவற்ற துயரற்ற உபநிடதத்தின் புகழுடன் அத்தியாயம் முடிகிறது.","ml":"അവ്യക്തത്തിനപ്പുറമുള്ള പരമത്തെക്കുറിച്ചുള്ള ജനകന്റെ ചോദ്യത്തിന് യാജ്ഞവൽക്യൻ മറുപടി നൽകുന്നു; ഗന്ധർവ്വനായ വിശ്വാവസുവുമായുള്ള കൂടിക്കാഴ്ചയെക്കുറിച്ചും അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു. കാലം, ജനനമില്ലാത്തത്, രണ്ടും ഒന്നിച്ചുള്ളവൻ എന്നിവയുടെ സ്വഭാവത്തെക്കുറിച്ച് വിശ്വാവസു ചോദ്യങ്ങൾ ചോദിക്കുന്നു. യാജ്ഞവൽക്യൻ ജനകന് നൽകിയ, മരണമില്ലാത്തതും ദുഃഖമില്ലാത്തതുമായ അമൃതുള്ള ഉപദേശത്തോടെ ഈ അധ്യായം അവസാനിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.306; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"मोक्षधर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Mokshadharma Parva (Duties for liberation)","verses":[{"text":"याज्ञवल्क्य उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yajnavalkya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"अव्यक्तस्थं परं यत्तत्पृष्टस्तेऽहं नराधिप ।\nपरं गुह्यमिमं प्रश्नं शृणुष्वावहितो नृप ॥","meaning":{"en":"You asked, king, about the supreme that abides in the unmanifest. Listen attentively to this question, most secret."}},{"n":2,"text":"यथार्षेणेह विधिना चरतावमतेन ह ।\nमयादित्यादवाप्तानि यजूंषि मिथिलाधिप ॥","meaning":{"en":"King of Mithila, I once obtained the Yajur Vedas from the Sun, following the rule of the sages in a way that was approved."}},{"n":3,"text":"महता तपसा देवस्तपिष्ठः सेवितो मया ।\nप्रीतेन चाहं विभुना सूर्येणोक्तस्तदानघ ॥","meaning":{"en":"By great austerity I served the god, the most blazing one; and the all-pervading Sun, pleased, said to me then, sinless one:"}},{"n":4,"text":"वरं वृणीष्व विप्रर्षे यदिष्टं ते सुदुर्लभम् ।\nतत्ते दास्यामि प्रीतात्मा मत्प्रसादो हि दुर्लभः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Choose a boon, brahmin sage, whatever you desire that is hard to obtain; being pleased I shall give it, for my grace is hard to get.\""}},{"n":5,"text":"ततः प्रणम्य शिरसा मयोक्तस्तपतां वरः ।\nयजूंषि नोपयुक्तानि क्षिप्रमिच्छामि वेदितुम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, bowing my head, I said to that best of the burning ones: \"I wish to know quickly the Yajus verses, which have not been used.\""}},{"n":6,"text":"ततो मां भगवानाह वितरिष्यामि ते द्विज ।\nसरस्वतीह वाग्भूता शरीरं ते प्रवेक्ष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the Lord said to me, \"I shall give them to you, brahmin: Sarasvati, as speech, will enter your body.\""}},{"n":7,"text":"ततो मामाह भगवानास्यं स्वं विवृतं कुरु ।\nविवृतं च ततो मेऽऽस्यं प्रविष्टा च सरस्वती ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the Lord told me, \"Open your mouth.\" When I opened my mouth, Sarasvati entered."}},{"n":8,"text":"ततो विदह्यमानोऽहं प्रविष्टोऽम्भस्तदानघ ।\nअविज्ञानादमर्षाच्च भास्करस्य महात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, sinless one, burning, I plunged into water, through lack of understanding and impatience with the great-souled Sun."}},{"n":9,"text":"ततो विदह्यमानं मामुवाच भगवान्रविः ।\nमुहूर्तं सह्यतां दाहस्ततः शीतीभविष्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the Lord Ravi said to me as I burned: \"Bear the burning for a moment; then you will be cool.\""}},{"n":10,"text":"शीतीभूतं च मां दृष्ट्वा भगवानाह भास्करः ।\nप्रतिष्ठास्यति ते वेदः सोत्तरः सखिलो द्विज ॥","meaning":{"en":"And seeing me cooled, the Lord Bhaskara said: \"Your Veda, brahmin, will stand firm, with its later part and its supplements.\""}},{"n":11,"text":"कृत्स्नं शतपथं चैव प्रणेष्यसि द्विजर्षभ ।\nतस्यान्ते चापुनर्भावे बुद्धिस्तव भविष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Best of brahmins, you will bring out the whole Shatapatha, and at its end you will have the thought of no rebirth.\""}},{"n":12,"text":"प्राप्स्यसे च यदिष्टं तत्सांख्ययोगेप्सितं पदम् ।\nएतावदुक्त्वा भगवानस्तमेवाभ्यवर्तत ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"And you will attain the desired state sought through Sankhya and Yoga.\" Having said this much, the Lord turned toward the setting hill."}},{"n":13,"text":"ततोऽनुव्याहृतं श्रुत्वा गते देवे विभावसौ ।\nगृहमागत्य संहृष्टोऽचिन्तयं वै सरस्वतीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, having heard what was said and the god of light having gone, I returned home delighted and thought of Sarasvati."}},{"n":14,"text":"ततः प्रवृत्तातिशुभा स्वरव्यञ्जनभूषिता ।\nओंकारमादितः कृत्वा मम देवी सरस्वती ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the goddess Sarasvati came to me, very auspicious, adorned with vowels and consonants, beginning with the syllable Om."}},{"n":15,"text":"ततोऽहमर्घ्यं विधिवत्सरस्वत्यै न्यवेदयम् ।\nतपतां च वरिष्ठाय निषण्णस्तत्परायणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then I duly offered the water of welcome to Sarasvati, and sat devoted to her, the best of the burning ones."}},{"n":16,"text":"ततः शतपथं कृत्स्नं सरहस्यं ससंग्रहम् ।\nचक्रे सपरिशेषं च हर्षेण परमेण ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then with supreme joy I composed the entire Shatapatha, with its secrets, its compendium and its remainder."}},{"n":17,"text":"कृत्वा चाध्ययनं तेषां शिष्याणां शतमुत्तमम् ।\nविप्रियार्थं सशिष्यस्य मातुलस्य महात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And having taught it to a hundred excellent pupils, to displease my great-souled maternal uncle with his pupils..."}},{"n":18,"text":"ततः सशिष्येण मया सूर्येणेव गभस्तिभिः ।\nव्याप्तो यज्ञो महाराज पितुस्तव महात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"...then, great king, with my pupils, like the sun with its rays, I filled the sacrifice of your great-souled father."}},{"n":19,"text":"मिषतो देवलस्यापि ततोऽर्धं हृतवानहम् ।\nस्ववेददक्षिणायाथ विमर्दे मातुलेन ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"And in the very sight of Devala I took away half of the fee, for my own Veda's fee, in a dispute with my uncle."}},{"n":20,"text":"सुमन्तुनाथ पैलेन तथा जैमिनिना च वै ।\nपित्रा ते मुनिभिश्चैव ततोऽहमनुमानितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Sumantu, Paila, Jaimini and your father, along with the sages, honored me."}},{"n":21,"text":"दश पञ्च च प्राप्तानि यजूंष्यर्कान्मयानघ ।\nतथैव लोमहर्षाच्च पुराणमवधारितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sinless one, I obtained fifteen Yajus verses from the Sun, and likewise took in the Purana from Lomaharshana."}},{"n":22,"text":"बीजमेतत्पुरस्कृत्य देवीं चैव सरस्वतीम् ।\nसूर्यस्य चानुभावेन प्रवृत्तोऽहं नराधिप ॥","meaning":{"en":"Placing this seed foremost, and the goddess Sarasvati, and by the Sun's power, I set to work, king..."}},{"n":23,"text":"कर्तुं शतपथं वेदमपूर्वं कारितं च मे ।\nयथाभिलषितं मार्गं तथा तच्चोपपादितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"...to make the Shatapatha Veda, and had it made as something unprecedented; it was accomplished along the path I wished."}},{"n":24,"text":"शिष्याणामखिलं कृत्स्नमनुज्ञातं ससंग्रहम् ।\nसर्वे च शिष्याः शुचयो गताः परमहर्षिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The whole of it, with its compendium, was entrusted to the pupils, and all the pupils went away pure and delighted."}},{"n":25,"text":"शाखाः पञ्चदशेमास्तु विद्या भास्करदर्शिताः ।\nप्रतिष्ठाप्य यथाकामं वेद्यं तदनुचिन्तयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"These are the fifteen branches shown by Bhaskara; having established them as I wished, I reflected on what is to be known."}},{"n":26,"text":"किमत्र ब्रह्मण्यमृतं किं च वेद्यमनुत्तमम् ।\nचिन्तये तत्र चागत्य गन्धर्वो मामपृच्छत ॥","meaning":{"en":"I thought, \"What here is the nectar in Brahman, and what is the unsurpassed thing to be known?\" And while I thought, a Gandharva came and questioned me."}},{"n":27,"text":"विश्वावसुस्ततो राजन्वेदान्तज्ञानकोविदः ।\nचतुर्विंशतिकान्प्रश्नान्पृष्ट्वा वेदस्य पार्थिव ।\nपञ्चविंशतिमं प्रश्नं पप्रच्छान्वीक्षिकीं तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, king, Vishvavasu, skilled in the knowledge of Vedanta, having asked twenty-four questions about the Veda, king, asked the twenty-fifth question as well, on reasoning."}},{"n":28,"text":"विश्वाविश्वं तथाश्वाश्वं मित्रं वरुणमेव च ।\nज्ञानं ज्ञेयं तथाज्ञो ज्ञः कस्तपा अतपास्तथा ।\nसूर्यादः सूर्य इति च विद्याविद्ये तथैव च ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Vishva and Avishva, the Ashva and Anashva, Mitra and Varuna; knowledge and the knowable, the ignorant and the knower, who is the ascetic and the non-ascetic; the one who eats the sun and the sun, knowledge and ignorance..."}},{"n":29,"text":"वेद्यावेद्यं तथा राजन्नचलं चलमेव च ।\nअपूर्वमक्षयं क्षय्यमेतत्प्रश्नमनुत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"...the knowable and the unknowable, king; the unmoving and the moving; the unprecedented, the imperishable and the perishable: this was the unsurpassed question."}},{"n":30,"text":"अथोक्तश्च मया राजन्राजा गन्धर्वसत्तमः ।\nपृष्टवाननुपूर्वेण प्रश्नमुत्तममर्थवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"And I, king, said to the king of the Gandharvas, who had asked the excellent, meaningful question in order:"}},{"n":31,"text":"मुहूर्तं मृष्यतां तावद्यावदेनं विचिन्तये ।\nबाढमित्येव कृत्वा स तूष्णीं गन्धर्व आस्थितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Be patient a moment while I reflect on this.\" \"So be it,\" said the Gandharva, and remained silent."}},{"n":32,"text":"ततोऽन्वचिन्तयमहं भूयो देवीं सरस्वतीम् ।\nमनसा स च मे प्रश्नो दध्नो घृतमिवोद्धृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then I thought again of the goddess Sarasvati in my mind, and that question rose for me like ghee drawn up from curd."}},{"n":33,"text":"तत्रोपनिषदं चैव परिशेषं च पार्थिव ।\nमथ्नामि मनसा तात दृष्ट्वा चान्वीक्षिकीं पराम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There, king, dear one, I churned in my mind the Upanishad and what remains, having seen the supreme science of reasoning."}},{"n":34,"text":"चतुर्थी राजशार्दूल विद्यैषा सांपरायिकी ।\nउदीरिता मया तुभ्यं पञ्चविंशेऽधि धिष्ठिता ॥","meaning":{"en":"This fourth science, tiger among kings, the one concerned with the beyond, I stated to you, resting on the twenty-fifth."}},{"n":35,"text":"अथोक्तस्तु मया राजन्राजा विश्वावसुस्तदा ।\nश्रूयतां यद्भवानस्मान्प्रश्नं संपृष्टवानिह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, king, I said to King Vishvavasu: \"Hear what you have asked of us here.\""}},{"n":36,"text":"विश्वाविश्वेति यदिदं गन्धर्वेन्द्रानुपृच्छसि ।\nविश्वाव्यक्तं परं विद्याद्भूतभव्यभयंकरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Lord of the Gandharvas, this 'Vishva and Avishva' that you ask about: know Vishva as the supreme unmanifest, terrifying to past and future.\""}},{"n":37,"text":"त्रिगुणं गुणकर्तृत्वादविश्वो निष्कलस्तथा ।\nअश्वस्तथैव मिथुनमेवमेवानुदृश्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Because it makes the qualities it is threefold, and the Avishva is partless. In the same way the Ashva and the pair are to be understood.\""}},{"n":38,"text":"अव्यक्तं प्रकृतिं प्राहुः पुरुषेति च निर्गुणम् ।\nतथैव मित्रं पुरुषं वरुणं प्रकृतिं तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"They call the unmanifest Nature, and the qualityless the Person; likewise the Person is Mitra, and Nature is Varuna.\""}},{"n":39,"text":"ज्ञानं तु प्रकृतिं प्राहुर्ज्ञेयं निष्कलमेव च ।\nअज्ञश्च ज्ञश्च पुरुषस्तस्मान्निष्कल उच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"They call Nature knowledge, and the partless the knowable; the Person, both ignorant and knowing, is therefore called partless.\""}},{"n":40,"text":"कस्तपा अतपाः प्रोक्तः कोऽसौ पुरुष उच्यते ।\nतपाः प्रकृतिरित्याहुरतपा निष्कलः स्मृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Who is the ascetic and the non-ascetic? Who is called the Person? They say the ascetic is Nature, and the non-ascetic is held to be the partless.\""}},{"n":41,"text":"तथैवावेद्यमव्यक्तं वेद्यः पुरुष उच्यते ।\nचलाचलमिति प्रोक्तं त्वया तदपि मे शृणु ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Likewise the unmanifest is the unknowable and the Person is called the knowable. Hear also what you called the moving and unmoving.\""}},{"n":42,"text":"चलां तु प्रकृतिं प्राहुः कारणं क्षेपसर्गयोः ।\nअक्षेपसर्गयोःकर्ता निश्चलः पुरुषः स्मृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"They call Nature moving, the cause of emission and creation; the Person is held to be motionless, the maker of non-emission and non-creation.\""}},{"n":43,"text":"अजावुभावप्रजौ च अक्षयौ चाप्युभावपि ।\nअजौ नित्यावुभौ प्राहुरध्यात्मगतिनिश्चयाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Both are unborn and without offspring, and both are imperishable; those certain of the course of the Self call both unborn and eternal.\""}},{"n":44,"text":"अक्षयत्वात्प्रजनने अजमत्राहुरव्ययम् ।\nअक्षयं पुरुषं प्राहुः क्षयो ह्यस्य न विद्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Because of imperishability in generation, they call the unborn here undying; they call the Person imperishable, for he has no decay.\""}},{"n":45,"text":"गुणक्षयत्वात्प्रकृतिः कर्तृत्वादक्षयं बुधाः ।\nएषा तेऽऽन्वीक्षिकी विद्या चतुर्थी सांपरायिकी ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The wise call Nature imperishable through being the maker, though the qualities decay. This is your fourth science of reasoning, concerned with the beyond.\""}},{"n":46,"text":"विद्योपेतं धनं कृत्वा कर्मणा नित्यकर्मणि ।\nएकान्तदर्शना वेदाः सर्वे विश्वावसो स्मृताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Having made wealth together with knowledge, through action in the daily rites, all the Vedas, Vishvavasu, are held to show a single view.\""}},{"n":47,"text":"जायन्ते च म्रियन्ते च यस्मिन्नेते यतश्च्युताः ।\nवेदार्थं ये न जानन्ति वेद्यं गन्धर्वसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Those who do not know the meaning of the Veda, the knowable, best of Gandharvas, in which these are born and die and from which they fall...\""}},{"n":48,"text":"साङ्गोपाङ्गानपि यदि पञ्च वेदानधीयते ।\nवेदवेद्यं न जानीते वेदभारवहो हि सः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"...even if they study the five Vedas with their limbs and subsidiary limbs, does not know what the Veda makes known; he is a mere bearer of the Veda's burden.\""}},{"n":49,"text":"यो घृतार्थी खरीक्षीरं मथेद्गन्धर्वसत्तम ।\nविष्ठां तत्रानुपश्येत न मण्डं नापि वा घृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Best of Gandharvas, one who wanting ghee churns the milk of a she-ass would see only dung there, neither cream nor ghee.\""}},{"n":50,"text":"तथा वेद्यमवेद्यं च वेदविद्यो न विन्दति ।\nस केवलं मूढमतिर्ज्ञानभारवहः स्मृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"So the one who has the learning of the Veda does not find the knowable and the unknowable; he is held to be only a fool bearing the burden of knowledge.\""}},{"n":51,"text":"द्रष्टव्यौ नित्यमेवैतौ तत्परेणान्तरात्मना ।\nयथास्य जन्मनिधने न भवेतां पुनः पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"These two are to be seen always, with the inner self intent on them, so that birth and death do not come again and again.\""}},{"n":52,"text":"अजस्रं जन्मनिधनं चिन्तयित्वा त्रयीमिमाम् ।\nपरित्यज्य क्षयमिह अक्षयं धर्ममास्थितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Having reflected on endless birth and death in this triple Veda, he abandons the perishable here and takes his stand in imperishable dharma.\""}},{"n":53,"text":"यदा तु पश्यतेऽत्यन्तमहन्यहनि काश्यप ।\nतदा स केवलीभूतः षड्विंशमनुपश्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"When, Kashyapa, he sees it fully day after day, then, become alone, he beholds the twenty-sixth.\""}},{"n":54,"text":"अन्यश्च शश्वदव्यक्तस्तथान्यः पञ्चविंशकः ।\nतस्य द्वावनुपश्येत तमेकमिति साधवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The one is always unmanifest, and the other is the twenty-fifth; the good see these two as one in him.\""}},{"n":55,"text":"तेनैतन्नाभिजानन्ति पञ्चविंशकमच्युतम् ।\nजन्ममृत्युभयाद्योगाः सांख्याश्च परमैषिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"For this reason, out of fear of birth and death, the Yogis and the Sankhyas who seek the highest do not recognize the twenty-fifth, the unfallen.\""}},{"text":"विश्वावसुरुवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vishvavasu said:"}},{"n":56,"text":"पञ्चविंशं यदेतत्ते प्रोक्तं ब्राह्मणसत्तम ।\nतथा तन्न तथा वेति तद्भवान्वक्तुमर्हति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Best of brahmins, what you have said about this twenty-fifth: whether it is so or not so, you should tell me.\""}},{"n":57,"text":"जैगीषव्यस्यासितस्य देवलस्य च मे श्रुतम् ।\nपराशरस्य विप्रर्षेर्वार्षगण्यस्य धीमतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I have heard of Jaigishavya, Asita, Devala, the brahmin sage Parashara, and the wise Varshaganya...\""}},{"n":58,"text":"भिक्षोः पञ्चशिखस्याथ कपिलस्य शुकस्य च ।\nगौतमस्यार्ष्टिषेणस्य गर्गस्य च महात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"...of the mendicant Panchashikha, of Kapila and Shuka, of Gautama, Arshtishena and the great-souled Garga...\""}},{"n":59,"text":"नारदस्यासुरेश्चैव पुलस्त्यस्य च धीमतः ।\nसनत्कुमारस्य ततः शुक्रस्य च महात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"...of Narada, Asuri, the wise Pulastya, then Sanatkumara and the great-souled Shukra...\""}},{"n":60,"text":"कश्यपस्य पितुश्चैव पूर्वमेव मया श्रुतम् ।\nतदनन्तरं च रुद्रस्य विश्वरूपस्य धीमतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"...of Kashyapa and of my father; and I heard it earlier, and after that from Rudra and the wise Vishvarupa.\""}},{"n":61,"text":"दैवतेभ्यः पितृभ्यश्च दैत्येभ्यश्च ततस्ततः ।\nप्राप्तमेतन्मया कृत्स्नं वेद्यं नित्यं वदन्त्युत ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"From the gods, from the ancestors and from the Daityas in turn I have received all this; they say the knowable is eternal.\""}},{"n":62,"text":"तस्मात्तद्वै भवद्बुद्ध्या श्रोतुमिच्छामि ब्राह्मण ।\nभवान्प्रबर्हः शास्त्राणां प्रगल्भश्चातिबुद्धिमान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Therefore, brahmin, I wish to hear it again according to your understanding; you are the foremost of the treatises, bold and very wise.\""}},{"n":63,"text":"न तवाविदितं किंचिद्भवाञ्श्रुतिनिधिः स्मृतः ।\nकथ्यते देवलोके च पितृलोके च ब्राह्मण ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Nothing is unknown to you; you are called the treasury of revelation, brahmin, in the world of the gods and in the world of the ancestors.\""}},{"n":64,"text":"ब्रह्मलोकगताश्चैव कथयन्ति महर्षयः ।\nपतिश्च तपतां शश्वदादित्यस्तव भाषते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The great sages who have gone to Brahma's world speak of it, and Aditya, the lord of the burning ones, always speaks of you.\""}},{"n":65,"text":"सांख्यज्ञानं त्वया ब्रह्मन्नवाप्तं कृत्स्नमेव च ।\nतथैव योगज्ञानं च याज्ञवल्क्य विशेषतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Brahmin, you have obtained the whole knowledge of Sankhya, and likewise especially the knowledge of Yoga, Yajnavalkya.\""}},{"n":66,"text":"निःसंदिग्धं प्रबुद्धस्त्वं बुध्यमानश्चराचरम् ।\nश्रोतुमिच्छामि तज्ज्ञानं घृतं मण्डमयं यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"You are awakened beyond doubt, awakening to all that moves and stands; I wish to hear that knowledge, as one wishes the cream from ghee.\""}},{"text":"याज्ञवल्क्य उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yajnavalkya said:"}},{"n":67,"text":"कृत्स्नधारिणमेव त्वां मन्ये गन्धर्वसत्तम ।\nजिज्ञाससि च मां राजंस्तन्निबोध यथाश्रुतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Best of Gandharvas, I consider you a holder of everything; since you wish to learn from me, hear it as it was heard.\""}},{"n":68,"text":"अबुध्यमानां प्रकृतिं बुध्यते पञ्चविंशकः ।\nन तु बुध्यति गन्धर्व प्रकृतिः पञ्चविंशकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The twenty-fifth awakens to Nature, which does not awaken; but, Gandharva, Nature does not awaken to the twenty-fifth.\""}},{"n":69,"text":"अनेनाप्रतिबोधेन प्रधानं प्रवदन्ति तम् ।\nसांख्ययोगाश्च तत्त्वज्ञा यथाश्रुतिनिदर्शनात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Because of this non-awakening, the Sankhyas and Yogis who know the principles call it the Primal, according to the tradition's illustration.\""}},{"n":70,"text":"पश्यंस्तथैवापश्यंश्च पश्यत्यन्यस्तथानघ ।\nषड्विंशः पञ्चविंशं च चतुर्विंशं च पश्यति ।\nन तु पश्यति पश्यंस्तु यश्चैनमनुपश्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Seeing and not seeing, sinless one, the other sees; the twenty-sixth sees the twenty-fifth and the twenty-fourth. But the one who sees does not see the one who watches him.\""}},{"n":71,"text":"पञ्चविंशोऽभिमन्येत नान्योऽस्ति परमो मम ।\nन चतुर्विंशकोऽग्राह्यो मनुजैर्ज्ञानदर्शिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The twenty-fifth thinks, 'There is none higher than I'; and the twenty-fourth is not to be grasped by men who see knowledge.\""}},{"n":72,"text":"मत्स्येवोदकमन्वेति प्रवर्तति प्रवर्तनात् ।\nयथैव बुध्यते मत्स्यस्तथैषोऽप्यनुबुध्यते ।\nसस्नेहः सहवासाच्च साभिमानश्च नित्यशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Like a fish following the water, it moves because of its movement; as the fish is aware, so this one is aware, affectionate through living together and always self-regarding.\""}},{"n":73,"text":"स निमज्जति कालस्य यदैकत्वं न बुध्यते ।\nउन्मज्जति हि कालस्य ममत्वेनाभिसंवृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"He sinks into time when he does not awaken to oneness, and rises through time, wrapped in the sense of mine.\""}},{"n":74,"text":"यदा तु मन्यतेऽन्योऽहमन्य एष इति द्विजः ।\nतदा स केवलीभूतः षड्विंशमनुपश्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"But when the brahmin thinks, 'I am other, and this is other,' then, become alone, he beholds the twenty-sixth.\""}},{"n":75,"text":"अन्यश्च राजन्नवरस्तथान्यः पञ्चविंशकः ।\nतत्स्थत्वादनुपश्यन्ति एक एवेति साधवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The one is other, king, and lower, and the twenty-fifth is another; the good see them as one because of standing in it.\""}},{"n":76,"text":"तेनैतन्नाभिनन्दन्ति पञ्चविंशकमच्युतम् ।\nजन्ममृत्युभयाद्भीता योगाः सांख्याश्च काश्यप ।\nषड्विंशमनुपश्यन्ति शुचयस्तत्परायणाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"For this reason, Kashyapa, the Yogis and Sankhyas, afraid of birth and death, do not delight in the twenty-fifth, the unfallen; pure and devoted to it, they behold the twenty-sixth.\""}},{"n":77,"text":"यदा स केवलीभूतः षड्विंशमनुपश्यति ।\nतदा स सर्वविद्विद्वान्न पुनर्जन्म विन्दति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"When, become alone, he beholds the twenty-sixth, then, all-knowing and wise, he finds no rebirth.\""}},{"n":78,"text":"एवमप्रतिबुद्धश्च बुध्यमानश्च तेऽनघ ।\nबुद्धश्चोक्तो यथातत्त्वं मया श्रुतिनिदर्शनात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"So, sinless one, the unawakened, the awakening and the awakened have been described to you truly by me from the illustration of the tradition.\""}},{"n":79,"text":"पश्यापश्यं योऽनुपश्येत्क्षेमं तत्त्वं च काश्यप ।\nकेवलाकेवलं चाद्यं पञ्चविंशात्परं च यत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"One who sees the seeing and the not-seeing, Kashyapa, sees safety and the principle, the alone and the not alone, the first, and what is beyond the twenty-fifth.\""}},{"text":"विश्वावसुरुवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vishvavasu said:"}},{"n":80,"text":"तथ्यं शुभं चैतदुक्तं त्वया भोः\nसम्यक्क्षेम्यं देवताद्यं यथावत् ।\nस्वस्त्यक्षयं भवतश्चास्तु नित्यं\nबुद्ध्या सदा बुद्धियुक्तं नमस्ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"True and auspicious is what you have said, sir, rightly salutary and first among the gods, as it is. May welfare and imperishability be yours always, wise one, ever joined with wisdom; I bow to you.\""}},{"text":"याज्ञवल्क्य उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yajnavalkya said:"}},{"n":81,"text":"एवमुक्त्वा संप्रयातो दिवं स\nविभ्राजन्वै श्रीमता दर्शनेन ।\nतुष्टश्च तुष्ट्या परयाभिनन्द्य\nप्रदक्षिणं मम कृत्वा महात्मा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having spoken thus, he went to heaven, shining with a glorious appearance, pleased, greeting me with great delight, and having circled me to the right, the great-souled one..."}},{"n":82,"text":"ब्रह्मादीनां खेचराणां क्षितौ च\nये चाधस्तात्संवसन्ते नरेन्द्र ।\nतत्रैव तद्दर्शनं दर्शयन्वै\nसम्यक्क्षेम्यं ये पथं संश्रिता वै ॥","meaning":{"en":"...showing there that vision of Brahma and the sky-farers, and of those on earth and those dwelling below, king, to those who have taken the path of safety."}},{"n":83,"text":"सांख्याः सर्वे सांख्यधर्मे रताश्च\nतद्वद्योगा योगधर्मे रताश्च ।\nये चाप्यन्ये मोक्षकामा मनुष्या-\nस्तेषामेतद्दर्शनं ज्ञानदृष्टम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"All the Sankhyas devoted to the Sankhya dharma, and likewise the Yogis devoted to the Yoga dharma, and other people who desire liberation: this is their vision, seen through knowledge."}},{"n":84,"text":"ज्ञानान्मोक्षो जायते पूरुषाणां\nनास्त्यज्ञानादेवमाहुर्नरेन्द्र ।\nतस्माज्ज्ञानं तत्त्वतोऽन्वेषितव्यं\nयेनात्मानं मोक्षयेज्जन्ममृत्योः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Liberation arises for people from knowledge; there is none from ignorance, they say, king. So knowledge should be sought in truth, by which one may free oneself from birth and death."}},{"n":85,"text":"प्राप्य ज्ञानं ब्राह्मणात्क्षत्रियाद्वा\nवैश्याच्छूद्रादपि नीचादभीक्ष्णम् ।\nश्रद्धातव्यं श्रद्दधानेन नित्यं\nन श्रद्धिनं जन्ममृत्यू विशेताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having gained knowledge from a brahmin or a kshatriya, a vaishya or even a shudra or lowly one, one should constantly trust it with faith; birth and death do not enter one who has faith."}},{"n":86,"text":"सर्वे वर्णा ब्राह्मणा ब्रह्मजाश्च\nसर्वे नित्यं व्याहरन्ते च ब्रह्म ।\nतत्त्वं शास्त्रं ब्रह्मबुद्ध्या ब्रवीमि\nसर्वं विश्वं ब्रह्म चैतत्समस्तम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"All castes are brahmins and born of Brahman; all always speak Brahman. I speak the principle and teaching with the understanding of Brahman; all this universe is Brahman."}},{"n":87,"text":"ब्रह्मास्यतो ब्राह्मणाः संप्रसूता\nबाहुभ्यां वै क्षत्रियाः संप्रसूताः ।\nनाभ्यां वैश्याः पादतश्चापि शूद्राः\nसर्वे वर्णा नान्यथा वेदितव्याः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brahmins were born from Brahma's mouth, kshatriyas from his arms, vaishyas from his navel, and shudras from his feet; all the castes are to be understood so and not otherwise."}},{"n":88,"text":"अज्ञानतः कर्मयोनिं भजन्ते\nतां तां राजंस्ते यथा यान्त्यभावम् ।\nतथा वर्णा ज्ञानहीनाः पतन्ते\nघोरादज्ञानात्प्राकृतं योनिजालम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Through ignorance they take up the womb of action; as, king, they go to whichever state, so the castes, lacking knowledge, fall from terrible ignorance into the net of natural wombs."}},{"n":89,"text":"तस्माज्ज्ञानं सर्वतो मार्गितव्यं\nसर्वत्रस्थं चैतदुक्तं मया ते ।\nतस्थौ ब्रह्मा तस्थिवांश्चापरो य-\nस्तस्मै नित्यं मोक्षमाहुर्द्विजेन्द्राः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Therefore knowledge should be sought everywhere; I have told you that it abides everywhere. For him who stands as Brahma and for the other who stands, the best of brahmins always declare liberation."}},{"n":90,"text":"यत्ते पृष्टं तन्मया चोपदिष्टं\nयाथातथ्यं तद्विशोको भवस्व ।\nराजन्गच्छस्वैतदर्थस्य पारं\nसम्यक्प्रोक्तं स्वस्ति तेऽस्त्वत्र नित्यम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"What you asked has been taught by me as it truly is; so be free of sorrow. King, go to the far shore of this matter; it has been rightly spoken. May you always have welfare here."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":91,"text":"स एवमनुशास्तस्तु याज्ञवल्क्येन धीमता ।\nप्रीतिमानभवद्राजा मिथिलाधिपतिस्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus instructed by the wise Yajnavalkya, the king, lord of Mithila, then became pleased."}},{"n":92,"text":"गते मुनिवरे तस्मिन्कृते चापि प्रदक्षिणे ।\nदैवरातिर्नरपतिरासीनस्तत्र मोक्षवित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When that best of sages had gone, and after he had circled him, King Devarati, the knower of liberation, remained seated there."}},{"n":93,"text":"गोकोटिं स्पर्शयामास हिरण्यस्य तथैव च ।\nरत्नाञ्जलिमथैकं च ब्राह्मणेभ्यो ददौ तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"He made a crore of cows and gold touch the brahmins, and then gave them one handful of jewels."}},{"n":94,"text":"विदेहराज्यं च तथा प्रतिष्ठाप्य सुतस्य वै ।\nयतिधर्ममुपासंश्चाप्यवसन्मिथिलाधिपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, having established his son in the kingdom of Videha, the lord of Mithila lived practicing the dharma of an ascetic."}},{"n":95,"text":"सांख्यज्ञानमधीयानो योगशास्त्रं च कृत्स्नशः ।\nधर्माधर्मौ च राजेन्द्र प्राकृतं परिगर्हयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"King of kings, studying the knowledge of Sankhya and the whole science of Yoga, he condemned dharma and adharma as natural."}},{"n":96,"text":"अनन्तमिति कृत्वा स नित्यं केवलमेव च ।\nधर्माधर्मौ पुण्यपापे सत्यासत्ये तथैव च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Regarding the alone as eternal and infinite, he thought of dharma and adharma, merit and sin, truth and untruth..."}},{"n":97,"text":"जन्ममृत्यू च राजेन्द्र प्राकृतं तदचिन्तयत् ।\nब्रह्माव्यक्तस्य कर्मेदमिति नित्यं नराधिप ॥","meaning":{"en":"...and birth and death, king of kings, as natural: \"This is the work of Brahma, the unmanifest,\" he thought, king, always."}},{"n":98,"text":"पश्यन्ति योगाः सांख्याश्च स्वशास्त्रकृतलक्षणाः ।\nइष्टानिष्टवियुक्तं हि तस्थौ ब्रह्म परात्परम् ।\nनित्यं तमाहुर्विद्वांसः शुचिस्तस्माच्छुचिर्भव ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Yogis and Sankhyas see this, each marked by their own treatises: Brahman, beyond the beyond, stands free of the wished-for and unwished-for. The wise call it eternal; so be pure, therefore."}},{"n":99,"text":"दीयते यच्च लभते दत्तं यच्चानुमन्यते ।\nददाति च नरश्रेष्ठ प्रतिगृह्णाति यच्च ह ।\nददात्यव्यक्तमेवैतत्प्रतिगृह्णाति तच्च वै ॥","meaning":{"en":"Best of men, what is given, what is received, what is permitted when given, what one gives and what one takes: all this gives the unmanifest and takes the unmanifest."}},{"n":100,"text":"आत्मा ह्येवात्मनो ह्येकः कोऽन्यस्त्वत्तोऽधिको भवेत् ।\nएवं मन्यस्व सततमन्यथा मा विचिन्तय ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Self alone is one for the Self; who else could be higher than you? Think so always, and do not think otherwise."}},{"n":101,"text":"यस्याव्यक्तं न विदितं सगुणं निर्गुणं पुनः ।\nतेन तीर्थानि यज्ञाश्च सेवितव्याविपश्चिता ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who has not known the unmanifest, with or without qualities, should resort, as one who knows little, to holy places and sacrifices."}},{"n":102,"text":"न स्वाध्यायैस्तपोभिर्वा यज्ञैर्वा कुरुनन्दन ।\nलभतेऽव्यक्तसंस्थानं ज्ञात्वाव्यक्तं महीपते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Joy of the Kurus, king, not by study, austerities or sacrifices does one reach the abode of the unmanifest; one must know the unmanifest."}},{"n":103,"text":"तथैव महतः स्थानमाहंकारिकमेव च ।\nअहंकारात्परं चापि स्थानानि समवाप्नुयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the same way one may reach the place of the great principle and that of egoism, and the places beyond egoism."}},{"n":104,"text":"ये त्वव्यक्तात्परं नित्यं जानते शास्त्रतत्पराः ।\nजन्ममृत्युवियुक्तं च वियुक्तं सदसच्च यत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"But those devoted to the treatises who know what is eternal beyond the unmanifest, free of birth and death, and free of the existent and non-existent..."}},{"n":105,"text":"एतन्मयाप्तं जनकात्पुरस्ता-\nत्तेनापि चाप्तं नृप याज्ञवल्क्यात् ।\nज्ञानं विशिष्टं न तथा हि यज्ञा\nज्ञानेन दुर्गं तरते न यज्ञैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I obtained this long ago from Janaka, and he obtained it from Yajnavalkya, king. This knowledge is distinguished; sacrifices are not so. One crosses the difficult by knowledge, not by sacrifices."}},{"n":106,"text":"दुर्गं जन्म निधनं चापि राज-\nन्न भूतिकं ज्ञानविदो वदन्ति ।\nयज्ञैस्तपोभिर्नियमैर्व्रतैश्च\nदिवं समासाद्य पतन्ति भूमौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, birth and death are difficult to cross, and those who know knowledge do not call them prosperity. Through sacrifices, austerities, restraints and vows, people reach heaven and fall again to earth."}},{"n":107,"text":"तस्मादुपासस्व परं महच्छुचि\nशिवं विमोक्षं विमलं पवित्रम् ।\nक्षेत्रज्ञवित्पार्थिव ज्ञानयज्ञ-\nमुपास्य वै तत्त्वमृषिर्भविष्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Therefore, king, worship the supreme, great, pure, auspicious, spotless, sacred liberation. By worshipping the sacrifice of knowledge, knowing the knower of the field, you will become a sage of truth."}},{"n":108,"text":"उपनिषदमुपाकरोत्तदा वै\nजनकनृपस्य पुरा हि याज्ञवल्क्यः ।\nयदुपगणितशाश्वताव्ययं त-\nच्छुभममृतत्वमशोकमृच्छतीति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus Yajnavalkya long ago recited the Upanishad to King Janaka, which, thus reckoned, leads to the auspicious, eternal and undying, to immortality and freedom from sorrow."}}]}]}